#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:2
msgid "polkit interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:4
msgid "The `polkit` interface provides daemons with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:5
msgid ""
"The permission to use the [polkit authorisation manager](https://"
"www.freedesktop.org/software/polkit/docs/latest/polkit.8.html) (_polkitd_)  "
"to make access control decisions for requests from unprivileged clients."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:6
msgid "The ability to install custom polkit rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:9
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:11
msgid ""
"**{ref}`Auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`**: "
"no</br> **{ref}`Super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-super-"
"privileged-interfaces>`**: yes</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:11
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:14
msgid "**Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:16
msgid ""
"**action-prefix** (plug):  indicate that all actions published by the snap "
"are equal to the action prefix or match `${action-prefix}.*` ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:17
msgid ""
"**install-rules** (plug, requires *snapd 2.69*):  a list of polkit rule "
"files (and their hash for integrity validation) to be installed on the "
"system. Each entry must contain:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:18
msgid "**name**: name of the polkit rule file to be installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:19
msgid ""
"**sha3-384**: RFC 4648 base 64 encoded sha3-384 hash of the specified rule "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:21
msgid ""
"**Note: At least one of `action-prefix` or `install-rules` attributes must "
"be set*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:23
msgid "Polkit actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:25
msgid ""
"To perform polkit authorisation checks, a daemon needs to do two things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:27
msgid ""
"Install a .policy file to `$SNAP/meta/polkit/${plug_name}.*.policy` "
"describing the actions it will use (codifying the type of administrative "
"access a user might be granted). Snapd will install the policy file when the "
"plug is connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:28
msgid ""
"Before performing administrative work on behalf of a client app, make a "
"`CheckAuthorization` D-Bus call to polkitd to ask if they have access. The D-"
"Bus call passes a string action ID describing the access, and a “subject” "
"struct describing the client application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:30
msgid ""
"There are two primary ways a daemon can describe the subject of the check:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:32
msgid ""
"For D-Bus daemons they can use a `system-bus-name` subject, sending the "
"unique bus name of the client app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:33
msgid ""
"For non-D-Bus daemons, they can use a `unix-process` subject, sending the "
"process ID (as retrieved through `SO_PEERCRED` or `SCM_CREDENTIALS`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:35
msgid ""
"See https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/proposal-add-polkit-and-polkit-agent-"
"interfaces-to-snapd/23876 for the original interface proposal and reasoning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:37
msgid "Polkit rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:39
msgid ""
"To install polkit rules to the host system, a snap has to include a .rules "
"file to `$SNAP/meta/polkit/${plug_name}.*.rules`. Snapd will install the "
"rule file when the plug is connected given that there is a corresponding "
"entry under `install-rules` with the same rule file name and the specified "
"integrity `sha3-384` hash matches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:41
msgid "Approval process for `install-rules`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:42
msgid ""
"For distribution via the [Snap store](https://snapcraft.io/store), snaps "
"that use the polkit interface with the `install-rules` attribute need an "
"approved {ref}`snap declaration <interfaces-process-for-aliases-auto-"
"connections-and-tracks>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:44
msgid "For acceptance, the publisher needs to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:45
msgid "Explain the rationale for installing the polkit rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:46
msgid "Attach the polkit rule file content."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:47
msgid ""
"Include the matching RFC 4648 base 64 encoded sha3-384 hash of the attached "
"rule file content."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:49
msgid "Code examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/polkit-interface.md:51
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
" polkit:\n"
"  action-prefix: org.example.foo\n"
"  install-rules:\n"
"      - name: polkit.bar.rules\n"
"        sha3-384: "
"2YM8oyXyE7xuXR07EXqUpixvr8duiJwgPQqhnxZgrBCU8ZSDowV0Gyujvs1j0-KR\n"
"\n"
"apps:\n"
" app:\n"
"  command: foo\n"
"  plugs: [polkit]\n"
msgstr ""

